susemora","id":32273722,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjczNzIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32273722?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora","html_url":"https://github.com/Jesusemora","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-23T04:26:59Z","updated_at":"2026-05-23T04:26:59Z","body":"> Doesn't this change bring back #119543\r\n\r\nNo. https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119551 fixed the performance by splitting the code into two methods, `_build_surfaces_smoothed` and `_build_surfaces_default`.\r\n`default` had the code from before the autosmooth PR, but `smoothed` used the entire code from the PR, which had two conditional branches, one which calculated autosmooth and one which did the work that `default` now does, and this was set to run when `angle < 0.1`.\r\n\r\nThe branching is not supposed to be there anymore since that should to be handled by `_build_surfaces_default`. Faces are supposed to be flat, but instead the lower performance default smooth is used.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4524151366/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimi